{"id":"chatcmpl-56f9c4aa-7148-4a42-a165-23a1298b02b6","object":"chat.completion","created":1795245164,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"{\n  \"highlights\": \"The task required identifying a lateralized finding (left vs. right lower lobe atelectasis) from a chest X-ray. The successful strategy involved querying a domain-specific expert tool for a descriptive localization, then corroborating with a grounded reporting tool to confirm laterality. Both sources agreed on the left lower zone, leading to the correct answer. The pattern emphasizes using multiple independent tools to cross-validate spatial findings.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When a task requires lateralization (left/right) of a finding, query a domain expert tool for a descriptive localization before committing to an answer.\",\n    \"Use a second, independent tool (e.g., grounded report) to corroborate the laterality and location from the first tool, reducing risk of single-source error.\",\n    \"For binary choice questions involving anatomical location, explicitly ask the tool to describe the location and laterality rather than directly asking for the diagnosis.\",\n    \"When both tools agree on the key spatial attribute (e.g., left lower zone), select the corresponding option with high confidence.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging interpretation\": \"Use a specialized expert model to describe findings and their anatomical location; then use a grounded reporting tool to confirm laterality and localization before answering.\",\n    \"Binary choice with spatial attributes\": \"Ask the tool to describe the location and laterality in free text, then map the description to the options; avoid asking the tool to directly pick an option.\",\n    \"Cross-validation of tool outputs\": \"When multiple tools are available, query at least two independent tools for the same critical attribute (e.g., laterality) and only answer when they agree.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm that the tool's description explicitly states the laterality (left/right) and anatomical zone (e.g., lower lobe).\",\n    \"Verify that the corroborating tool's output is consistent with the first tool's localization before finalizing the answer.\"\n  ]\n}"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":449,"total_tokens":856,"completion_tokens":407,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":449},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":407}}}